    {
      "number": 20,
      "id": "I_kwDOMB0Qas6oCQoj",
      "title": "Taxonomy: tag placement",
      "url": "https://github.com/ietf-wg-dult/threat-model/issues/20",
      "state": "OPEN",
      "author": "maggiedelano",
      "authorAssociation": "COLLABORATOR",
      "assignees": [
        "exploretechsafety"
      ],
      "labels": [],
      "body": "Elaborate on tag placement and how that might impact the threat model, attacks, etc.:\n\n- Tag placed on victim\u2019s person or immediate belongings\n- Tag(s) in proximity to victim but not on their person (e.g. child\u2019s backpack, car)\n- Tags nearby but not used for unwanted location tracking (e.g. false positives by family or on transit)\n",
      "createdAt": "2025-01-29T20:09:02Z",
      "updatedAt": "2025-01-29T20:10:23Z",
      "closedAt": null,
      "comments": []
    },
    {
      "number": 21,
      "id": "I_kwDOMB0Qas6oCQ9p",
      "title": "Taxonomy: Anticipation of unwanted location tracking",
      "url": "https://github.com/ietf-wg-dult/threat-model/issues/21",
      "state": "OPEN",
      "author": "maggiedelano",
      "authorAssociation": "COLLABORATOR",
      "assignees": [
        "maggiedelano"
      ],
      "labels": [],
      "body": "Update the taxonomy to discuss the victim's self-assessed likelihood of being tracked:\n\n- Support for potential victims who are actively looking for potential tags (i.e. active scanning)\n- Support for potential victims who are not actively looking for potential tags (i.e. passive notifications)\n",
      "createdAt": "2025-01-29T20:09:49Z",
      "updatedAt": "2025-01-29T20:38:47Z",
      "closedAt": null,
      "comments": []
    },
    {
