    {
      "number": 26,
      "id": "I_kwDOMB0Qas6oCURh",
      "title": "Discuss proposed requirements for tracking system",
      "url": "https://github.com/ietf-wg-dult/threat-model/issues/26",
      "state": "OPEN",
      "author": "maggiedelano",
      "authorAssociation": "COLLABORATOR",
      "assignees": [],
      "labels": [],
      "body": "Discuss specific proposed requirements for the tracking system, for example:\n\n- Users should be able to actively scan their location for devices that might be tracking them\n- Protocol should be able to detect an unwanted location tracker passively within X minutes \n- Tags that are separated from their owners should notify nearby users (how and how often?)\n- Users should be able to customize their settings\n- Platform should assist user in locating trackers\n- Users should be able to disable tracker\n",
      "createdAt": "2025-01-29T20:16:42Z",
      "updatedAt": "2025-01-29T20:16:42Z",
      "closedAt": null,
      "comments": []
    },
    {
      "number": 27,
      "id": "I_kwDOMB0Qas6oCVXt",
      "title": "Requirement: Users should be able to actively scan their location for devices that might be tracking them",
      "url": "https://github.com/ietf-wg-dult/threat-model/issues/27",
      "state": "OPEN",
      "author": "maggiedelano",
      "authorAssociation": "COLLABORATOR",
      "assignees": [],
      "labels": [],
      "body": "Update the document to include a requirement that \"users should be able to actively scan their location for devices that might be tracking them.\"\n\nDiscuss key parameters such as ideal scan duration, when a scan should be able to be triggered, and when not to include a found device in a scan (e.g. devices that are near their owners).",
      "createdAt": "2025-01-29T20:18:13Z",
      "updatedAt": "2025-01-29T20:18:13Z",
      "closedAt": null,
      "comments": []
    },
