    {
      "number": 36,
      "id": "I_kwDOMB0Qas6oCjqU",
      "title": "Discuss possible design tradeoffs",
      "url": "https://github.com/ietf-wg-dult/threat-model/issues/36",
      "state": "OPEN",
      "author": "maggiedelano",
      "authorAssociation": "COLLABORATOR",
      "assignees": [],
      "labels": [],
      "body": "Detecting unwanted location tracking is often discussed as a trade off between privacy of unassociated tag owners and security of tracking victims (see e.g. [this article](https://eprint.iacr.org/2023/1332.pdf)). However, victims could be threatened using either attacks related to [remote advertisement monitoring](https://github.com/ietf-wg-dult/threat-model/issues/17) as well as the \"standard\" tracking scenario. Update the document to discuss this, and how the protocol should prioritize different types of attacks, victims, etc.",
      "createdAt": "2025-01-29T20:36:41Z",
      "updatedAt": "2025-01-29T20:36:41Z",
      "closedAt": null,
      "comments": []
    }
